---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Subscriptions, Billing & Refunds — Pre"
  description="How subscriptions, billing, cancellation, and refunds work for Pre."
>
  <main style="background-color: var(--color-bg); min-height: 100svh;">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm font-medium"
          style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);"
        >&larr; Back to Pre</a>
        <h1
          class="mb-4 font-sans text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl"
          style="color: var(--color-text);"
        >Subscriptions, Billing &amp; Refunds</h1>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);">
          Effective date: May 21, 2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-prose" style="font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--color-text);">

        <p>
          Confusing billing is the worst. Here's the short version: Pre's subscriptions are sold through
          the Apple App Store, so Apple — not us — handles the actual charging, renewals, and refunds.
          This page explains how all of that works and how to manage it.
        </p>

        <h2>How subscriptions work</h2>
        <p>
          Some of Pre's features need a paid subscription. When you subscribe, you're buying it through
          the Apple App Store using your Apple ID. Apple charges your payment method, and we use
          RevenueCat to keep track of your subscription status so the app knows what you have access to.
          We never see or store your card details — that's all on Apple's side. Apple collects any
          applicable taxes, such as VAT, as part of your purchase.
        </p>

        <h2>Free trials and auto-renewal</h2>
        <p>
          Some subscription plans may include a free trial or introductory offer. If one's available for
          the plan you pick, we'll show you the exact length, who's eligible, and the price after the
          trial — before you confirm. Subscriptions renew automatically: unless you cancel at least 24
          hours before the trial or current period ends, Apple charges your Apple ID the price shown at
          sign-up when the period ends, and the subscription renews until you cancel.
        </p>

        <h2>How to manage or cancel</h2>
        <p>
          Because Apple runs the billing, you cancel through your Apple account, not through us.
          Canceling stops the next renewal; you keep access until the end of the period you've already
          paid for. On your iPhone or iPad:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Open the <strong>Settings</strong> app and tap your name at the top</li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Subscriptions</strong></li>
          <li>Select <strong>Pre</strong></li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Cancel Subscription</strong> (or change your plan)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can also manage subscriptions from the App Store app or at
          <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions" style="color: var(--color-accent);">apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Since your purchase goes through the App Store, refunds are handled by Apple under
          <strong>their</strong> refund policy — we aren't able to process App Store refunds ourselves.
          To request one, go to
          <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" style="color: var(--color-accent);">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>,
          sign in with your Apple ID, find the Pre charge, and choose the option to request a refund.
          Apple decides whether to grant it.
        </p>
        <p>
          That said, if you've been charged by mistake or something's gone wrong, we still want to know.
          Write to us at
          <a href="mailto:support@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">support@trypre.app</a>
          and we'll help however we can — including pointing you to the right place and, where it's in
          our power, making it right.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you're a consumer in the EEA or UK, you may have a statutory right to withdraw from a
          purchase within 14 days — though that right usually ends once a subscription period or
          digital content has started with your consent. Apple administers these requests.
        </p>

        <h2>Price changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we ever change subscription prices, Apple will notify you in line with their rules, and in
          most cases you'll need to agree before a higher price takes effect. You can always cancel
          before a change kicks in if a new price isn't for you.
        </p>

        <h2>The rest of the fine print</h2>
        <p>
          This page works alongside our
          <a href="/terms" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Terms of Service</a> and
          <a href="/privacy" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Privacy Policy</a>. Your use of the App
          Store is also governed by Apple's own terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Stuck on anything billing-related? Email
          <a href="mailto:support@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">support@trypre.app</a>
          and we'll sort it out with you.
        </p>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-prose a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
